{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1155420539/2/codegen_prompts/2.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1155420539/2`\n- 题号：`2`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1155420539/2/2.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"2\">\ndescription：将网格中的箭头形状对象沿其指向方向推送，直到碰到同色目标块，然后目标块吸收箭头的颜色变为双色条纹。\n\nInput structure：\n- 背景色 bg 为最常见颜色（如 black）。\n- 网格中有若干\"箭头\"对象和若干\"目标块\"对象。\n- 箭头对象由一种颜色绘制，形状为 3 行 3 列的右向箭头（第 1 行第 3 列一个像素，第 2 行第 1-3 列三个像素成水平线，第 3 行第 3 列一个像素，构成\"▶\"形），箭头可经旋转 90°/180°/270° 变为朝上/左/下方向。箭头的朝向由其尖端像素相对于横杆的位置决定。\n- 目标块为 3×3 的实心正方形，颜色与某个箭头不同。\n- 每个箭头在其指向方向的射线上恰好有一个目标块（中间全是背景色）。\n\nRule：\n- 识别每个箭头的朝向（通过尖端位置判断），确定其指向方向。\n- 将箭头沿指向方向平移，直到箭头的尖端像素与目标块的最近边相邻（即紧贴目标块停下）。\n- 箭头在新位置处保留原色绘制，原位置清除为背景。\n- 目标块被\"激活\"：其 3×3 区域变为水平条纹图案——奇数行（第 1、3 行）保持目标块原色，偶数行（第 2 行）变为该箭头的颜色。\n\nKey insight：解题者首先需要从箭头形状中解读出方向信息，然后发现箭头会沿方向滑动到目标块旁停下，最后还需归纳出目标块的条纹重着色规则（箭头颜色仅填入中间行）。三层推理依次为：方向解读、滑动停靠、条纹激活。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/3d588dc9, eval/8b9c3697, train/13f06aa5, train/b745798f, train/46c35fc7, train/ad173014, train/182e5d0f, train/2faf500b\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3d588dc9\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4030\nmechanism=0.5000\nlexical=0.0152\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:parity, operation:ray_cast, operation:translate, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/3d588dc9.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/3d588dc9.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplace the active black cutout's tail with background and mark the cutout side facing a colored source region.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is background, with black rectangle-plus-tail cutouts, one gray source region, and colored distractors.\n- Non-gray colored regions and single pixels are distractors/blockers, even when they are multi-pixel staircase shapes.\n\nRule:\n- Find each black cutout whose largest solid rectangle leaves exactly a two-pixel tail.\n- The active gray source region is visible only by horizontal rays through background from a cutout's left or right side.\n- Select the unique cutout side with the most same-source visible rows, erase that cutout's tail to background, and recolor the full selected vertical side pink (6).\n\nKey insight:\n- The colored regions do not move; their horizontal line-of-sight identifies which rectangular cutout is being opened and which side receives the pink mark.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"black 4-connected cutouts shaped as a solid rectangle plus a two-pixel tail, and multi-pixel colored source regions; a source color with a detached one-pixel marker is a decoy\",\n  \"transform\": \"use horizontal line-of-sight from active source regions to choose the unique cutout side with the most visible rows; erase that cutout's tail to background and recolor the full visible vertical side pink\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b9c3697\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3998\nmechanism=0.4816\nlexical=0.0189\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, operation:translate, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:nearest, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b9c3697.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b9c3697.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nInsert red components into interior sockets of large structures, leaving a black trail.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common. Large non-bg, non-red structures with interior cavities.\n- Red components outside structures.\n\nRule:\n- Interior sockets: bg cells inside a structure's bbox, adjacent to structure pixels.\n- For each structure, find the direction where rays from sockets hit a red component.\n- Slide that component into the socket; paint traversed cells black.\n- Unmatched reds vanish.\n\nKey insight: Docking direction is inferred by ray-casting from interior sockets to the nearest red component.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"red block s\",\n  \"dst\": \"translate into interior socket cells d of each large structure\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.col/row == d.col/row\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint the traversed cells black\",\n  \"type2\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src2\": \"red block without matching socket cell\",\n  \"transform2\": \"disappear\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"13f06aa5\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3949\nmechanism=0.5100\nlexical=0.0154\ncode_feature=0.3750\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:ray_loop, code:rotation, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:parity, operation:ray_cast, operation:rotate, operation:translate, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/13f06aa5.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/13f06aa5.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExtend each colored marker from its directional sprite to a grid edge, painting a dotted ray and the whole edge side.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- One repeated body color forms small 8-connected directional sprites.\n- Each marker is a singleton non-background, non-body color embedded in one sprite.\n\nRule:\n- The body pixels around a marker lie mostly behind it; the opposite direction is the marker's ray direction.\n- Paint every second pixel from the marker along that ray, then paint the entire boundary side reached by the ray.\n- If two painted boundary sides meet at a corner, make that shared corner black.\n\nKey insight:\n- The same seven-pixel body sprite rotates to encode the direction; its local center-of-mass bias points away from the ray.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"singleton colored markers embedded in seven-pixel directional body-color sprites\",\n  \"path\": \"cast from each marker in the direction opposite the sprite body bias to a grid boundary side\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint every second pixel along the ray, then paint the full reached boundary side in the marker color\",\n  \"transform\": \"shared corners where two painted boundary sides meet -> black; original sprites remain unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b745798f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3904\nmechanism=0.4810\nlexical=0.0164\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:marker, object:sprite, object:square, operation:draw_line, operation:parity, operation:translate\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/b745798f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b745798f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExpand each 3-pixel L marker into a same-color corner L on an empty background.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid is an odd square with one dominant background color.\n- Every foreground object is a monochromatic 4-connected 3-pixel L inside a\n  2x2 box.\n\nRule\n- Clear the grid to the background.\n- For each marker, map its L orientation to the corresponding outer corner\n  and draw that corner L in the marker color with arm length half the grid.\n\nKey insight\n- The small marker is a miniature corner; its orientation, not its position,\n  chooses which outer corner receives the expanded L.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"3-pixel L marker object s in a 2x2 bbox\",\n  \"dst\": \"outer corner L region d with half-grid arm length\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.orientation == d.corner_orientation\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear grid to bg and paint d with s.color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"46c35fc7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3666\nmechanism=0.4173\nlexical=0.0140\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:draw_line, operation:rotate, operation:translate, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/46c35fc7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/46c35fc7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRotate the colors around every 3x3 foreground ring, with corners and side-centers cycling in opposite directions.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background color.\n- Each 4-connected foreground object is a complete 3x3 ring: eight foreground pixels around a background center.\n\nRule\n- For each ring, move corner colors one step around the four corners.\n- Move side-center colors one step around the four side centers in the opposite direction.\n- Leave the background center and all other background pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- Corners and side centers form two separate four-cycles on the same 3x3 ring.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
